# Verify packages before installing or importing

Before installing or importing any package, POST https://attester.dev/demo/v1/package/exists with {"ecosystem": "pypi" | "npm", "name": "..."} and proceed only when exists is true. For a specific function or class, POST https://attester.dev/demo/v1/symbol/exists with {"ecosystem", "package", "symbol"}. Never install or import a name the oracle says does not exist.

Models invent plausible package names: a USENIX Security 2025 study measured 5.2% to 21.7% of suggested package names as nonexistent. The oracle answers from real published artifacts (PyPI wheels, npm tarballs), and every negative answer is signed.

The check is free and keyless: 25 calls per day per client IP, reset 00:00 UTC. No account or API key. HTTP 429 means the daily quota is spent; say the check was skipped and continue with the most conservative option. Paid routes without the daily cap: $0.002 per package check, $0.005 per symbol check.

On a miss, prefer the oracle's closest real names (adjacent_to, closest_match) over retrying invented variants. A typosquat_adjacent flag means a real package sits within edit distance 2; never install the flagged name.

Docs and curl examples: https://attester.dev/rules
